%N A145757 Number of n X n binary arrays with all ones connected only either three adjacent vertically or three adjacent horizontally.
%C A145757 a(14)-a(20) were computed with Tally, a counting program written and proved correct in Lean 4: the statement that the program returns the number of n X n binary arrays of this kind is a theorem checked by the Lean kernel, and each value a(n) is a Lean theorem obtained by running the compiled program inside the proof (native_decide). The values were confirmed by an independent unverified Rust program based on a different automaton. - _Stefan Szeider_, Oct 13 2026
%H A145757 Stefan Szeider, <a href="/A145757/b145757.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..20</a>
